---
// ar-va.com: who I am and what I make (2026-11-28, user: the main domain is the landing page; brand.ar-va.com stays the
// reference for the design language and how the leaf is drawn). Written as Artur, in the first person. Positioning:
// .agents/product-marketing.md. The blog's list returns here when the blog is public again (shared/site.ts).
import Layout from '@shared/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Writing from '../components/Writing.astro';
import { MAIN_SITE_PUBLIC } from '@shared/site';

const products = [
  {
    name: 'music.ar-va.com', href: 'https://music.ar-va.com', status: '', line: 'Record shelves for people who don’t collect',
    text: 'Discogs lists every pressing and catalogue number, which collectors need and their friends skip. music.ar-va.com shows the same collection as covers on a shelf, and each album page plays the album.',
  },
  {
    name: 'vincent.ar-va.com', href: 'https://vincent.ar-va.com', status: '', line: 'Nextcloud themes from your colours',
    text: 'Nextcloud’s own settings take a single colour. Vincent builds a full light and dark theme from yours and checks every text colour for contrast; you copy the settings and CSS into Nextcloud.',
  },
  {
    name: 'anon.ar-va.com', href: 'https://anon.ar-va.com', status: '', line: 'Anonymous messages to me',
    text: 'A single text box with no sign-in. You write, I answer, and the answer stays behind your private link unless you ask me to publish it.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Solaris', href: '', status: 'In progress', line: 'Software for tattoo studios',
    text: 'One system for a studio’s artists, manager and front desk. It isn’t public yet.',
  },
];

const link = 'text-kikyo-600 dark:text-kikyo-400 underline underline-offset-3 hover:text-zinc-900 dark:hover:text-white';
const body = 'text-lg text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-pretty';
const h2 = 'font-bold text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-zinc-900 dark:text-white';
---
<Layout title="ARVA: digital craft, evermore" description="I’m Artur. Under the name ARVA I build web software for people the usual tools leave out: record shelves for friends who don’t collect, Nextcloud themes from your colours, anonymous messages, and Solaris for tattoo studios.">
  <main class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 w-full pt-12 pb-24">
    <header class="max-w-3xl">
      <div>
        <h1 class="font-bold text-5xl sm:text-6xl leading-[1.05] text-zinc-900 dark:text-white text-balance">Digital craft, evermore</h1>
        <p class={`mt-6 max-w-2xl text-xl text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-pretty`}>
          I’m Artur. Under the name ARVA I build web software for people the usual tools leave out: the friend who doesn’t
          collect records, the Nextcloud admin who isn’t a designer, the person with something hard to say.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="work">
      <h2 id="work" class={h2}>The work</h2>
      <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {products.map((p) => (
          <li class:list={['relative rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 bg-white dark:bg-night-surface p-6', p.href && 'hover:border-zinc-500 has-[a:focus-visible]:outline-2 has-[a:focus-visible]:outline-offset-2 has-[a:focus-visible]:outline-kikyo-500']}>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-xl text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">
                {p.href ? <a href={p.href} class="after:absolute after:inset-0 focus-visible:outline-none">{p.name}</a> : p.name}
              </h3>
              {p.status && <span class="rounded-md bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">{p.status}</span>}
            </div>
            <p class="mt-1 font-medium text-zinc-800 dark:text-zinc-200">{p.line}</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-pretty">{p.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="habits">
      <h2 id="habits" class={h2}>How I work</h2>
      <div class={`mt-4 max-w-3xl space-y-4 ${body}`}>
        <p>
          Most tools are built for people who already know the subject. I start from the person who doesn’t, and cut until
          they can use it on their first visit.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most of my time goes into the part nobody sees. On music.ar-va.com the record turns at 33⅓ rpm and the needle
          drop is a sound generated in the browser. Vincent’s test suite runs about a thousand generated themes through
          every contrast check. Visitors aren’t meant to notice any of it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where the software could decide for you, it leaves the decision with you. Vincent gives you the settings instead
          of touching your server, and anon publishes a message only when its writer asks.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20 max-w-3xl" aria-labelledby="leaf">
      <h2 id="leaf" class={h2}>The leaf</h2>
      <p class={`mt-4 ${body}`}>
        My sign is a <i>kashiwa</i> leaf, from a Japanese oak that keeps its dry leaves all winter and drops them only
        when the new ones open. That is where “evermore” comes from.
      </p>
      <p class={`mt-4 ${body}`}>
        <a class={link} href="https://brand.ar-va.com/story">How the leaf is drawn from 18 circles</a> and <a class={link} href="https://brand.ar-va.com/">the rules all my products follow</a> are on brand.ar-va.com.
      </p>
    </section>

    {MAIN_SITE_PUBLIC && <div class="mt-20"><Writing /></div>}
  </main>
</Layout>
